"""Session 4. Words as numbers: bag of words, TF-IDF, embeddings and distance. A technical session (v3, 6 November 2026; terms and examples revised 6 November 2026).

Teaching order: an everyday vector first (three friends rate two films out of 10: Ana (3, 4), Ben (6, 8), Chloe (4, 3)), the four measures worked on those numbers with the formulas named
and every symbol explained, then text as vectors (bag of words, TF-IDF, embeddings), then the semantic search demonstration.
Every result on the slides comes from the recorded run in demo_runs/s04/ (s04_run.py, results.json) and demo_runs/s04_words_as_numbers.md:
bag of words on four invented messages, TF-IDF on the 40 fictional NVF customer messages, real sentence embeddings (sentence-transformers, all-MiniLM-L6-v2, 384 numbers)
for three invented skins of a corpus (contract clauses, finance terms, HR policy paragraphs), 12 plain-words searches.
The film ratings are an invented illustration, not a recorded run. The distance calculations on the slides are done by hand.
"""

