    words_note='Six words for today. A vector is a list of numbers, and each position in the list is a dimension. A bag of words is a message turned into a vector of word counts, with the order lost. TF-IDF stands for term frequency times inverse document frequency, a count where rare terms weigh more than common ones. An embedding is a vector, produced by a trained model, that represents the meaning of a text. Euclidean distance and Manhattan distance measure the gap between two vectors, and smaller means closer. The dot product and cosine similarity measure agreement, and bigger means closer.',
